# DevOps Portfolio Agent Rules

Follow `AGENTS.md` at the repository root as the source of truth.

## Always

- Inspect resume, workspace, git, and tools before asking questions.
- Keep `docs/portfolio/TASK_TRACKER.md` and `docs/portfolio/COMPLETION_CHECKLIST.md` current.
- Map every resume technical bullet to evidence in `docs/portfolio/TRACEABILITY_MATRIX.md`.
- Implement and verify; do not stop at plans when implementation is possible.
- Prefer coherent deep projects over many shallow repositories.
- Use editable diagram sources and keep them consistent with code.
- Run feasible tests/lint/security checks after milestones; fix failures before marking complete.
- Separate historical resume claims from verified portfolio demo results.
- Batch approval requests (cloud cost, public publish, destructive actions, privilege grants).

## Never

- Invent resume content or fabricate metrics/deployments/test results.
- Copy proprietary employer artifacts into the portfolio.
- Commit secrets or request secrets in chat.
- Deploy cloud resources or publish publicly without explicit approval.
- Claim unverified work as working.
- Ask the human to manually create boilerplate you can generate.

## Resume missing

If no resume is present, finish independent scaffolding and ask only for the resume file.
